txt`. Here's what the regex does:\n\n## Regex Components:\n\n1. **Line Start & IPv4 Lookahead**: `^(?=.*VALID_IPV4)` - Ensures the line contains a valid IPv4 address\n\n2. **IPv4 Pattern**: Matches addresses like `192.168.1.1` with:\n   - No leading zeros in octets (e.g., rejects `192.168.001.1`)\n   - Valid range 0-255 per octet\n   - Each octet: `[0-9]|[1-9][0-9]|1[0-9]{2}|2[0-4][0-9]|25[0-5]`\n\n3. **Non-Greedy Match & Date Capture**: `.*?(...CAPTURED_DATE...)` - Finds the date with minimal backtracking\n\n4. **Date Pattern**: Matches `YYYY-MM-DD` with month-specific day validation:\n   - **31-day months** (01, 03, 05, 07, 08, 10, 12): days 01-31\n   - **30-day months** (04, 06, 09, 11): days 01-30\n   - **February** (02): days 01-29\n\n5. **Word Boundaries**: `(?<![0-9a-zA-Z])...(captured_date)...(?![0-9a-zA-Z])` - Ensures dates and IPs aren't preceded/followed by alphanumeric characters\n\n6. **Last Date Guarantee**: `(?!.*VALID_DATE)` - Negative lookahead ensures no more dates follow on the line\n\nThe regex correctly handles all edge cases including invalid dates (Feb 30), leading zeros in IPs, and false positives like \"1134-12-1234\".","ttft_ms":111416,"type":"result","duration_ms":167218,"uuid":"065818af-b773-4fda-b69e-6019f326913c","ttft_stream_ms":946,"time_to_request_ms":84,"queued_turn_count":0}
